      },
      ":question/id": "28e9089c-6417-5772-a8b3-173523505655",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify $\\cos(t-\\pi)$ in terms of $\\sin t$ or $\\cos t$.\n\nUse the difference formula\n\n$$\n\\cos(u-v)=\\cos u\\cos v+\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nand the exact values $\\cos\\pi=-1$ and $\\sin\\pi=0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Apply the difference formula with $u=t$ and $v=\\pi$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(t-\\pi)&=\\cos t\\cos\\pi+\\sin t\\sin\\pi\\\\\n&=\\cos t\\cdot(-1)+\\sin t\\cdot0\\\\\n&=-\\cos t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sine term vanishes; the cosine term changes sign."
    }
