      ":question/id": "31388341-544f-5e6b-8fe8-8155a0101cd5",
      ":question/problem": "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(-345^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(60^\\circ\\right)-\\sin\\left(-345^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recognize the sum formula in reverse:\n\n$$\n\\cos x\\cos y-\\sin x\\sin y=\\cos(x+y).\n$$\n\nCombining the angles gives\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(-345^\\circ+60^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(-285^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\nChoose a decomposition into special angles:\n\n$$\n-285^\\circ=30^\\circ-315^\\circ.\n$$\n\nRecall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x-y)=\\cos x\\cos y+\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(-285^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(30^\\circ-315^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(315^\\circ\\right)+\\sin\\left(30^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(315^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{- \\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
  },
