      ":question/id": "23700599-02b8-5b30-905e-86d4d7a86aa5",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n4\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right).\n$$\nUse $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=\\frac{\\pi}{16}$ and then with $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Group a factor of $2$ with the first sine\u2013cosine pair:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=2\\left[2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\right)\\right]\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\\n&=2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe new sine has the same angle as the remaining cosine, so apply the identity again:\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\n=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"
    }
  },
