      ":question/id": "f64ce496-30b9-55e2-87e9-3300b3fffed3",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify $\\cos(x-300^\\circ)-2\\cos(x+60^\\circ)$ using $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter signed coefficients.\n\n{{field-1}} $\\sin x+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use $\\cos(u-v)=\\cos u\\cos v+\\sin u\\sin v$ with $u=x$ and $v=300^\\circ$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(x-300^\\circ)&=\\cos x\\cos 300^\\circ+\\sin x\\sin 300^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\sin x\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v$ with $u=x$ and $v=60^\\circ$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos(x+60^\\circ)&=\\cos x\\cos 60^\\circ-\\sin x\\sin 60^\\circ\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\sin x\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDistribute the outside factors, then collect the sine and cosine terms. Let $E$ denote the original expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=1\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad -2\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(1\\cdot\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)+-2\\cdot\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right)\\sin x\\\\\n&\\quad+\\left(1\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+-2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\right)\\cos x\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\sin x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and the second is $- \\frac{1}{2}$."
    }
