      ":question/id": "bf5d2462-3174-5e60-a7b0-a4fd39f0ece8",
      ":question/problem": "Express $8\\cos^4(18^\\circ)-8\\cos^2(18^\\circ)+1$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Regroup the expression so that the alternative double-angle formula can be used twice. To check the regrouping, write $u=\\cos^2(18^\\circ)$:\n\n$$\n2(2u-1)^2-1=2(4u^2-4u+1)-1=8u^2-8u+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&8\\cos^4(18^\\circ)-8\\cos^2(18^\\circ)+1\\\\\n&\\qquad=2\\left(2\\cos^2(18^\\circ)-1\\right)^2-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)$ first at $x=18^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2(18^\\circ)-1=\\cos(36^\\circ).\n$$\n\nSubstitute this into the regrouped expression, then use the same identity at $x=36^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\left(2\\cos^2(18^\\circ)-1\\right)^2-1&=2\\cos^2(36^\\circ)-1\\\\\n&=\\cos(2\\cdot36^\\circ)\\\\\n&=\\cos(72^\\circ).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth applications are needed: $\\cos(36^\\circ)$ replaces only the inner expression."
    }
  },
