      ":question/id": "7557cacf-886f-55fb-9076-1837e9a0913c",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-332138",
      ":question/problem": "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {cos}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}\\right)-{sin}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}\\right)=\n$$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{\\cos }^{2}\u2061x-{\\sin }^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}\\right)-{sin}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}\\right) & =\\cos \\,\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{8}\\right) \\\\  & =\\cos \\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
