      ":question/id": "eda88667-03a3-54d2-bc45-5bd8cd910c52",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-24488",
      ":question/problem": "Express $$\n\\displaystyle {\\cos }^{2}\u2061\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right)-{\\sin }^{2}\u2061\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right)\n$$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{\\cos }^{2}\u2061x-{\\sin }^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\cos }^{2}\u2061\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right)-{\\sin }^{2}\u2061\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
