      ":question/id": "85585a6b-0c0e-5963-819c-40902d9e809c",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-142025",
      ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(x+\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\right)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{4\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\left(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\left(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{2}-\\sqrt{3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
